        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Popular Science, Girlfriends\n- People: Edward Livingston Youmans\n- Places: San Francisco, Coeymans, New York, New York City\n- Topics: magazines, popular science, lesbian perspective media\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Livingston Youmans was born in Coeymans, New York, on June 3, 1821.\n- Edward Livingston Youmans was an American scientific writer, editor, and lecturer who founded Popular Science magazine.\n- Girlfriends was a women's magazine that provided critical coverage of culture, entertainment, and world events from a lesbian perspective.\n- Girlfriends was published monthly from San Francisco beginning in 1993 and was distributed nationwide by Disticor.\n- Popular Science, also known as PopSci, is an American bi-monthly magazine that publishes popular science content for general readers on science and technology subjects.\n- Girlfriends ceased publication in 2006.\n- Edward Livingston Youmans died in New York City on January 18, 1887.",
